NetHack 5.0 for Atari System V and AMIX
=======================================

NetHack 5.0 (the m68k-wip branch of github.com/NetHack/NetHack) built as
a static AMIX program.  On Atari System V it runs through the service
pack's amx module (github.com/slaapliedje/atari-sysv-sp1).

    nethack         play in the terminal
    nethack -x      play in an X window with tiles (DISPLAY must be set)

Other arguments go to the game (-u name, -p role, -D ...).  Options go in
~/.nethackrc or $NETHACKOPTIONS; see Guidebook.txt here.

Installed files:

    /opt/nethack/bin/nethack    the command (/usr/bin/nethack links to it)
    /opt/nethack/lib/           the program, its data, tiles, X resources
                                and sysconf (who may use wizard mode, ...)
    /opt/nethack/doc/           this file, the Guidebook, the licence
    /var/opt/nethack/           scores, logs, saved games, bones: made on
                                first play, kept by pkgrm

Install as root:   pkgadd -d nethack-VERSION.pkg NETHACK
Remove:            pkgrm NETHACK

The game directory is open to every user (mode 0777): the program is not
set-group-id, so anyone on the machine can edit the score file.

Source: github.com/slaapliedje/asv-games has the build scripts, the
source changes and the exact upstream commit.  NetHack is under the
NetHack General Public License (the file "license" here).
